8. Direct P1 lifecycle smoke with non-zero spread, impact, and commission: `entry, scale_out,
   add_on, exit` produced remaining-lot basis `103.4335517842`; transaction actions were `BUY,
   SELL, ADD, SELL`; canonical fills were `BUY, SELL, BUY, SELL`; closed-trade P&L and fill-cash P&L
   both rounded to `2616.30`; ending cash was `102616.30`; and `_validate_episodes` passed.

## Self-review

- Confirmed add-on decisions occur only after completed-session exit/state processing and never
  fill at the signal close.
- Confirmed identity remap precedes gap-stop/full-exit cancellation and all BUY work.
- Confirmed missing exact opens remain pending, invalid opens terminate, and checkpoint removal
  follows successful execution so resume cannot execute twice.
- Confirmed stop price is never lowered; actual fill price drives weighted-average entry and risk.
- Confirmed an add-on after a partial exit uses only the surviving quantity and cost basis, while
  preserving already-realized scale-out P&L and exact fill-cash reconciliation.
- Confirmed candidate risk/cap requests cannot bypass cash, engine risk, aggregate size, or count
  ceilings.
- Confirmed transaction `ADD` does not alter the diagnostics-owned BUY/SELL fill schema.
- Confirmed V2's existing-position skip and legacy checkpoint/result framing remain unchanged.
- Confirmed no tests were created or modified.
